{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>Do not go up, etc.</b> He gave them two reasons to prevent them from going up: the first is that HaShem is not among them, and since this is so, this constitutes rebellion against HaShem — and you will find that the verse says in Mishneh Torah (Deuteronomy 1:43): ״וָאֲדַבֵּר אֲלֵיכֶם וְלֹא שְׁמַעְתֶּם וַתַּמְרוּ אֶת פִּי ה׳״; and the second reason: ״וְלֹא תִּנָּגְפוּ לִפְנֵי אוֹיְבֵיכֶם״ — the fear of the enemy."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:09:37.143452847Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}